; =============================================================================
; SECTION DIRECTORY + PRESET DATA BANKS (0x800000 - 0x82FFFF)
; =============================================================================
; First 192KB of the Table Data flash ROM: a 34-entry directory of 4-byte
; little-endian pointers (33 section pointers + null terminator) followed by
; the preset/user data banks the pointers describe.  Directory targets are
; NOT in address order: entry 7 points backward into this half and entries
; 6 and 28-32 point forward into the UI-bitmap half of the ROM (0x91D000-
; 0x92DDA0, still inside includes/wallpaper1_to_icons.bin -- kept numeric
; below until that blob is split).  A section's size is the distance to the
; next-higher directory target.
;
; This region is the rewritable user-data area of the table-data flash pair:
; the firmware's flash primitives unlock the chip with AMD command cycles at
; 0x815554/0x80AAA8 (chip word addresses 0xAAAA/0x5554 -- these fall inside
; sections 25 and 10 but are command writes, not data references), and
; "Technics KN5000 Table    DATA FILE 1/2" update floppies rewrite the whole
; 0x800000 half via HANDLE_UPDATE_FILE_TYPE_ID_003h -> Flash_BurnWithProgress
; + FDC_WriteSectors (maincpu boot/system_handlers.s).  No disassembled
; maincpu/subcpu code reads an individual directory entry or section address
; directly, so the per-section roles below are described structurally; the
; factory images here are the power-on/factory-reset defaults for the user's
; sound/registration/composer memories (exact mapping still unattributed).
;
; FILL-PATTERN LEGEND (factory-default state of each bank):
;   0xF7/0xF8  erased-flash background patterns
;   0x07/0x06  default parameter values
;   0x00       zeroed fields        0xFF/0xFE/0xFC  empty/erased fields
;
; RECORD GRIDS (dominant autocorrelation stride, all exact size divisors):
;   sec 0/1: 95 x 120 B     sec 3-5: 222 x 22 B    sec 8: 25 x 112 B
;   sec 9: 18 x 80 B        sec 10: 25 x 114 B     sec 11: 20 x 108 B
;   sec 12-24: 52 x 58 B (13 uniform slots)   sec 25-27: 108 x 296 B
;
; SECTION ACCESSORS (established 2026-09-25): this ROM itself carries 17
; small routines at 0x82F000-0x82F2E8 (SectionInfo_SecNN, at the end of
; this module) that return, for directory entries 0-11 and 28-32, the
; section base (selector 0), the record size or bitmap width (1) and the
; record count or bitmap height (2).  Their constants confirm the grids of
; sections 0-11 above (section 10: 113-byte records on a 114-byte stride)
; and show that entries 6, 7 and 28-32 are 8bpp bitmaps; entries 12-27
; have no accessor.  Entry 7 is the "KN-5000" wordmark, not a data bank.
; This file was bootstrapped by scripts/generators/generate_preset_banks.py
; (commit e50f3c99) and has been hand-maintained since; regenerating it
; would discard the section 7 / accessor conversion.
; =============================================================================

SectionDirectory_Table:
	.long	PresetBank_Sec00		; entry  0:  11,400 B
	.long	PresetBank_Sec01		; entry  1:  11,400 B
	.long	PresetBank_Sec02		; entry  2:   1,764 B
